 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 671625,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>The genetic code is based on each amino acid being coded for by a distinctive series of three nucleic acid bases in mRNA called a codon. The following is a short segment of DNA using the slash symbol ( / ) to separate the base triplets that are transcribed in codons for easy viewing:</p>\n\n<div data-math=\"\\text{ATC/GTT/GAA/CTG/TAG/GAT/AAA}\">\\text{ATC/GTT/GAA/CTG/TAG/GAT/AAA}</div>\n\n<p>A change has occurred in the segment resulting in the following:</p>\n\n<div data-math=\"\\text{ATC/GTT/GTA/CTG/TAG/GAT/AAA}\">\\text{ATC/GTT/GTA/CTG/TAG/GAT/AAA}</div>\n\n<p>What kind of change has occurred?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1342927,
     "content_html": "A substitution of <span data-math=\"\\text{T}\">\\text{T}</span> for <span data-math=\"\\text{A}\">\\text{A}</span>, changing the coding for the third codon"
    },
    {
     "id": 1342928,
     "content_html": "An addition of <span data-math=\"\\text{C}\">\\text{C}</span> for <span data-math=\"\\text{G}\">\\text{G}</span>, lengthening the strand and changing every codon past the addition"
    },
    {
     "id": 1342929,
     "content_html": "A deletion of an <span data-math=\"\\text{A}\">\\text{A}</span>, resulting in a shortening and changing every codon past the deletion"
    },
    {
     "id": 1342930,
     "content_html": "No change has occurred; the same one base was replaced with the same one"
    }
   ],
